# Prime Occupation Partitions: An Interactive Journey

Prime numbers can be treated as independent energy modes. Each prime $p$ receives weight $p^{-\beta}$, and an occupation number records its exponent in an integer. Begin with the [Euler product](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euler_product) and the [geometric series](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geometric_series), then explore how two finite cutoffs affect the answer.

## 1. Watch an occupation defect decay

The first widget compares the exact relative defect $1-\prod_i(1-q_i^{N+1})$ with the additive certificate $\sum_i q_i^{N+1}$.

