<details><summary>Reveal the exact factorization and proof idea</summary>
For each mode, $\sum_{n=0}^Nq_i^n=(1-q_i^{N+1})/(1-q_i)$. Multiplication over the finite mode set gives $T_N=C\prod_i(1-q_i^{N+1})$. The inequality $1-\prod_i(1-a_i)\le\sum_i a_i$ follows by induction and yields the certified bound.
</details>

## 2. Turn primes into modes

Adjust the cutoff and temperature. The smallest prime contributes the largest first-omitted weight and therefore usually controls occupation convergence.

