<details><summary>Reveal the arithmetic interpretation</summary>
An occupation vector $(n_p)$ encodes the integer $m=\prod_pp^{n_p}$ by [unique factorization](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fundamental_theorem_of_arithmetic). Its total weight is $m^{-\beta}$. The prime cutoff restricts allowed prime divisors; the occupation ceiling restricts their exponents.
</details>

